      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Federal Arbitration Act (FAA) sets forth procedures for enforcing arbitration agreements in federal court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 3 of the FAA, entitled \u201cStay of proceedings where issue therein referable to arbitration,\u201d provides that when a dispute is subject to arbitration, the court \u201cshall on application of one of the parties stay the trial of the action until such arbitration has been had in accordance with the terms of the agreement, providing the applicant for the stay is not in default in proceeding with such arbitration.\u201d 9 U. S. C. \u00a7 3."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents insist that \u201cstay\u201d \u201cmeans only that the court must stop parallel in-court litigation, which a court may achieve by dismissing,\u201d Brief for Respondents 15,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Association for Justice",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Briefs of amici curiae urging affrmance were fled for the American Association for Justice by Jeffrey R. White and Sean Domnick;"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "New England Legal Foundation",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "and for the New England Legal Foundation by Benjamin G. Robbins and Daniel B. Winslow."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They sued respondents in Arizona state court, alleging violations of federal and state employment laws."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "After removing the case to federal court, respondents moved to compel arbitration and dismiss the suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners conceded that all of their claims were arbitrable, but they argued that \u00a7 3 of the FAA required the District Court to stay the action pending arbitration rather than dismissing it entirely ."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ninth Circuit",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0010",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit affrmed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0011",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court granted certiorari to answer the question it previously left open and resolve the Circuit split."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e75b081189b42def82bc3104957a2f23724d448b465686fba5e4d075d0cd59ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e75b081189b4-0000-0012",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it avoids costs and complications that might arise if a party were required to bring a new suit and pay a new fling fee to invoke the FAA's procedural protections."
